WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
A spark lands in dry grass.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.630
It flickers, smoulders, and dies.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.030
Southern California, January 2025.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.110
The Eaton fire breaks out.

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:19.450
In 2023, fires worldwide released an
estimated 2,100 megatonnes of carbon.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.070
Every fire needs fuel, oxygen and heat.

7
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.450
So why does one fire go out, while
another burns through a city?

8
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.550
In this mission, you'll
test fuel, climate,

9
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.830
recent weather and fire
behaviour, one by one.

10
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.510
Then you'll weigh
natural and human causes,

11
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.550
from lightning to people.

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: explain why one fire goes
out while another burns through a city.
